      "id": 1,
      "text": "In the late 1800s, Fairview residents formed a historical society to safeguard pioneer stories and artifacts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/fairview-museum/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By the early 20th century, the Fairview Museum’s collection had outgrown its temporary storage, prompting expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/fairview-museum/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1970s environmental movement inspired Fairview Museum to create a dedicated natural history section.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/fairview-museum/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Around 1920, the McMillan family donated land and funds, allowing construction of the museum’s first purpose‑built wing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/fairview-museum/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The 1960s art gallery wing, finished in the early 1980s, now displays Fairview’s geological formations, native plants, and wildlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wonderfulmuseums.com/museum/fairview-museum/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today, the Fairview Museum serves as a public commons where children and historians alike connect with the town’s evolving story.",
